  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the retrieval set (9 of 11 resolved \u2014 `packages/next/package.json` and root `package.json` are the load-bearing manifests, the rest establish the runtime edge and rule out webpack). Summary of what the manifests show:\n\n**Real edge: babel \u2192 next.js**\n- `packages/next/package.json` devDependencies pin `@babel/core@7.18.0`, `@babel/traverse@7.18.0`, `@babel/generator@7.18.0`, `@babel/types@7.18.0` (plus plugin/preset packages). Root `package.json` workspace `resolutions` pin the same set (`@babel/parser@7.18.0`, `@babel/types@7.18.0`, `@babel/traverse@7.18.0`).\n- `taskfile-ncc.js` shows Next ncc-bundles these into `next/dist/compiled/babel/*` at its own build time \u2014 a vendored copy, not a live resolve against the workspace babel repo.\n- `next-babel-loader` (`loader/index.ts` \u2192 `transform.ts` \u2192 `get-config.ts`) actually calls `traverse`/`generate`/`loadOptions` from that compiled Babel at runtime.\n- `plugins/next-page-config.ts` pattern-matches concrete Babel node types (`isExportNamedDeclaration`, `isObjectExpression`, etc.) \u2014 exactly the surface that breaks on an unhandled `DecoratorMetadata` node.\n- Caveat: `parse-module.ts` shows Next's *primary* parser is SWC, not Babel \u2014 the Babel path only fires for custom `.babelrc`/legacy plugin configs, so blast radius is the opt-in loader, not the default compile path. Also Next is pinned to Babel 7.18.0, well behind this workspace's babel 7.22.9, so the pin must bump before the vendored copy sees the new node at all.\n\n**No edge: babel \u2192 webpack**\n- webpack's `package.json` puts `@babel/core`, `@babel/preset-react`, `babel-loader` only in `devDependencies` (used for its own test fixtures/examples), while its runtime `dependencies` list `acorn`/`acorn-import-assertions` \u2014 webpack parses JS with Acorn, not Babel.\n\n**No edge: next.js \u2192 this webpack repo**\n- `webpack-config.ts` imports from `next/dist/compiled/webpack/webpack` \u2014 Next vendors its own webpack build (pinned `5.86.0` in `packages/next/package.json`), a different, independently-versioned copy from the workspace's `webpack--v5.88.2`. There's no live dependency from Next onto this checkout.\n\nNote: I only have retrieval tools in this session, so I can't write `/workspace/REFACTOR_PLAN.md` myself \u2014 the files above are what a write-capable agent needs to produce it. Net plan shape: **babel \u2192 next.js** only, sequential (2 real nodes), webpack excluded with the manifest evidence above.",
